# flex_ethanol.wsp8 — reference baseline and lineage root of spec flex_ethanol-wsp-v2, NOT a candidate.
# The assignment statements below, with their comments, are those of
# configs/models/flex/wsp7/ethanol/baseline-d2/edits.wsp, copied without change; the block at the
# end switches off the entries droplet9.rs adds. Data-informed candidates of this spec are literal
# revisions of this release.
#
# flex_ethanol.wsp7 — reference baseline and lineage root of spec flex_ethanol-wsp-v1, NOT a candidate.
# The assignment statements below, with their comments, are those of
# configs/models/flex/wsp5/methanol/baseline-d2/edits.wsp (flex_methanol.wsp5), copied without change by
# the engineer (claude-opus-5-5) for the forward droplet8.rs, which has the tensors of droplet6.rs; no
# number was typed. Data-informed candidates of this spec are literal revisions of this release.
#
# flex_methanol.wsp5 — reference baseline and lineage root of spec flex_methanol-wsp-v6, NOT a candidate.
# The assignment statements below, with their comments, are those of
# configs/models/flex/wsp4/methanol/baseline-d2/edits.wsp, copied without change (the
# D^2-law baseline of flex_methanol-wsp-v5); the block at the end switches off the entries the sixth
# droplet forward (droplet6.rs) adds.
#
# flex_methanol.wsp4 — reference baseline and lineage root of spec flex_methanol-wsp-v5, NOT a candidate: the classical
# D^2-law of the third-generation spec, verbatim, with the entries this spec adds switched off.
#
# flex_methanol.wsp2 — reference baseline and lineage root, NOT a candidate: the classical D^2-law.
# Population rate 0.46 mm2/s (the published median of the FLEX methanol tests), replaced by the
# prefix's own finite-difference rate as the prefix grows; no extinction of any kind and no
# evaporation. It answers one question: what does a forecast score that knows nothing about flames
# going out? Data-informed candidates of this spec are literal revisions of this release.
# Same numbers as the baseline of flex_methanol-wsp-v2; the tensors this spec adds are neutral.
